# VRAM preset for a 24GB AMD card on ROCm (validated on a 7900 XTX,
# gfx1100, ROCm 7.2.4, torch 2.13.0+rocm7.2). Same nominal VRAM class as
# presets/24GB.env (tuned for an RTX 4090/CUDA) but NOT a drop-in swap -
# this card needed real changes to fit, documented below. Sources the CUDA
# preset first for everything else (CHUNK_SIZE, MAX_RES, etc. all transfer
# fine - see that file for the full reasoning on each), then overrides only
# what this card measured differently.
#
# Usage:
#   source presets/24GB-7900xtx-rocm.env && ./run_stereo.sh input.mp4
# or, since run_season.sh sources a preset itself:
#   PRESET=24GB-7900xtx-rocm.env ./run_season.sh source_video/<season_dir>

SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
# shellcheck disable=SC1091
source "$SCRIPT_DIR/24GB.env"

# CONFIDENCE: measured directly on this card, 2026-08-31.
#
# ATTENTION_SLICING=False (set by 24GB.env itself as of this session) is
# worth just as much here as on CUDA - confirmed via a direct sdpa_kernel
# probe that this card (gfx1100/RDNA3, unlike the RX 6700 XT/RDNA2 dev
# card) has a real working flash/efficient-attention kernel in ROCm 7.2.
# Steady-state (after both the UNet's and the VAE decoder's one-time MIOpen
# kernel-tuning cost - see below) measured 0.70s/frame end-to-end
# (CHUNK_SIZE=210, MAX_RES=768, CLASSICAL_ONLY=True), actually faster than
# the 4090's own documented 0.96s/frame - though that 4090 number was very
# likely ALSO run with the ATTENTION_SLICING bug still present (never
# fixed in 24GB.env until this session), so this isn't a real hardware
# comparison, just confirmation this card's number is good enough to use.
#
# BUT: 24GB.env's own STAGE1_DECODE_CHUNK_SIZE=16 (validated safe on the
# 4090 at ~22GB/24.5GB peak, ~2.5GB headroom) genuinely OOM'd on THIS card
# with ATTENTION_SLICING=False - peaked at 23/23GB then failed allocating
# ~2.8GB with only ~2.9GB free. Same nominal settings, less real headroom
# on this card - unclear why (driver/runtime overhead, kernel scratch
# memory, OS reservation all plausible, not verified which). Dropping to 8
# fixed it with the 0.70s/frame steady-state number above.
#
# Now 2, not 8: that 0.70s/frame measurement was taken at CHUNK_SIZE=210.
# CHUNK_SIZE=1580 below is ~7.5x more frames held per outer chunk, which
# eats the headroom 8 was relying on. Lowered by the user on the real card;
# only the VAE decode step is affected (cheap relative to the depth UNet),
# so the throughput cost should be small - but the 0.70s/frame figure above
# no longer describes this configuration and has not been re-measured.
export STAGE1_DECODE_CHUNK_SIZE=2

# MIOpen note (not a setting, just worth remembering when reading timing
# off this card): the FIRST chunk run on a fresh box pays real one-time
# kernel-tuning costs the CUDA preset never has to think about - separately
# for the UNet's attention/conv shapes (~25 min observed cold) and the VAE
# decoder's own shapes (~6 min observed cold, first time that phase was
# ever reached). Both are cached to disk (~/.cache/miopen) and don't repeat
# on later chunks or later runs - don't judge this card's real speed off a
# first-chunk timing, always use a second (or later) chunk's number.

# ---- stage 1, this card's own values (set by the user on the real box).
#
# CHUNK_SIZE deliberately overrides 24GB.env's 210. That 210 was measured on
# a rented 4090 for ~90% VRAM utilisation with ~2.5GB headroom, and its own
# header argues CHUNK_SIZE barely moves peak VRAM at MAX_RES=768 (halving it
# recovered only ~1GB) because the cost is dominated by DepthCrafter's fixed
# per-window attention at WINDOW_SIZE=70, not by how many windows chain into
# one outer chunk. 1580 is what the splat stores in outputs/ were actually
# built with. Bigger outer chunks mean fewer chunk-boundary crossfade seams
# in the depth map; the tradeoff is the reduced decode headroom noted above.
export CHUNK_SIZE=1580

# decord (stage 1's VideoReader) gives up on a seek after a fixed number of
# EOF retries and returns short/garbage reads on some containers. Raising the
# cap is the standard workaround. Env var, read by decord itself, not by any
# script in this repo - which is why it belongs here rather than in
# run_stereo.sh's own knob list.
export DECORD_EOF_RETRY_MAX=20480

# Asymmetric silhouette expansion. The full-res expansion after the depth
# upsample runs as two passes and they are separate trades, not one
# symmetric knob (see depth_splatting_inference.py's EXPAND_RIGHT /
# EXPAND_OTHER): a disocclusion only ever opens on an object's RIGHT, so
# that is the one side where growing the foreground classification both
# fixes a real misclassification AND leaves a hole for stage 2 to fill.
# Growing the other directions relocates artifacts instead of removing them.
# Only RIGHT is set: OTHER inherits run_stereo.sh's EDGE_FILL_ITERS default
# of 2, so this is the 4/2 configuration, not 4/unset.
export EDGE_FILL_ITERS_RIGHT=4

# ---- stage 2: classical fill only.
#
# CLASSICAL_ONLY=True skips the SVD inpainting model entirely (it is never
# even loaded - no model-load time, no VRAM) and ships cv2.INPAINT_TELEA
# over the splat holes. Chosen after A/B'ing the diffusion path on real
# footage: it looked better, and the diffusion path costs ~16.5 s/output-
# frame on this card, i.e. ~156 hours for a 34096-frame episode.
#
# WORK_SCALE still matters even with no model running, which is not
# obvious: read_chunk does the TELEA prefill AT the working resolution and
# the classical path then upsamples that back to full res. At 0.5 you get a
# half-resolution fill bicubic-upscaled into full-res holes; at 1.0 the fill
# is computed at full res. It costs nothing on the GPU either way - the
# prefill is CPU/OpenCV - so there is no reason to run it at 0.5.
export CLASSICAL_ONLY=True
export WORK_SCALE=1.0

# Everything the diffusion path needs is deliberately NOT set here:
# TILE_NUM, FRAMES_CHUNK, NUM_INFERENCE_STEPS, MIN/MAX_GUIDANCE_SCALE,
# PREFILL_OCCLUSION, RESCUE_THRESHOLD, DECODE_LATENTS_CHUNK_SIZE,
# AGGRESSIVE_FREE. With CLASSICAL_ONLY=True none of them do anything -
# prefill_occlusion is forced True, and the tiling/denoising/VAE-decode code
# never runs. RESCUE_THRESHOLD would be worse than useless: the rescue pass
# sits after the mask gate on BOTH paths, so it would spend a full extra
# TELEA pass per chunk rescuing TELEA with TELEA.
#
# To use the diffusion path, source presets/quality-1080p.env AFTER this
# file. Do NOT just flip CLASSICAL_ONLY=False - 24GB.env's WORK_SCALE=0.5
# would then apply, and at that scale the holes are under one latent pixel,
# so the model reproduces its conditioning and you pay full GPU price for
# the same classical fill this preset already gives you for free.
